          "theme": "The Arrest of Rosa Parks",
          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> **Municipal Bus Segregation in Montgomery:** In Montgomery, Alabama, municipal bus segregation was a daily humiliation for Black residents, who made up over 70% of passengers. Black riders had to pay at the front, enter through the rear, and give up their seats in the middle section if white rows filled up. Drivers carried pistols and routinely shouted racial abuse at Black passengers.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[1.2]</span> **The Arrest of Rosa Parks (1 Dec 1955):** On 1 December 1955, seamstress and NAACP activist Rosa Parks refused a driver's order to give her seat to a white man. Her arrest triggered immediate action: Jo Ann Robinson and the Women’s Political Council printed 35,000 leaflets calling for a one-day boycott on 5 December, launching the historic Montgomery Bus Boycott."
