          "theme": "The Anniston & Montgomery Ambush",
          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> **Robert Kennedy Deploys Federal Marshals:** The violence in Alabama embarrassed President John F. Kennedy during the Cold War. Attorney General Robert Kennedy deployed 400 federal marshals to protect riders in Montgomery, Alabama, after local police abandoned them to another violent white mob at the bus terminal.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> **The ICC Desegregation Order (Nov 1961):** Robert Kennedy petitioned the Interstate Commerce Commission (ICC) to enforce compliance. On 1 November 1961, the ICC issued strict nationwide regulations ordering the removal of all \"whites only\" signs in interstate bus and train terminals, proving that non-violent direct action could force the federal government to act."
