          "title": "The Detroit & Newark Rebellions",
          "theme_heading": "The Detroit & Newark Rebellions",
          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> The urban crisis peaked during the \"Long Hot Summer\" of 1967, when major **Detroit & Newark riots (1967)** exploded across industrial cities. In Newark, twenty-six people died following the police beating of a Black cab driver. In Detroit, an early morning police raid on an unlicenced drinking club sparked five days of catastrophic street warfare, looting, and arson.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> The devastation resulted in **43 dead in Detroit violence**, two thousand injuries, and seven thousand arrests, prompting President Lyndon Johnson to dispatch **Federal airborne paratroopers** with armored tanks to suppress the rebellion. The scale of destruction proved that inner-city African Americans felt completely abandoned by mainstream American society, turning to destructive urban rebellions as a desperate cry for social justice.",
