          "title": "The Overthrow & Assassination of Diem",
          "theme_heading": "The Overthrow & Assassination of Diem",
          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.1]</span> By late 1963, President John F. Kennedy realized that Diem's oppressive governance was actively sabotaging the anti-communist war effort. Discontented South Vietnamese military officers plotted a coup, seeking American approval before moving against the palace. Through ambassador Henry Cabot Lodge Jr., the Kennedy administration provided covert assurances that Washington would not interfere with a military takeover.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.2]</span> On 1 November 1963, the **Saigon military coup (1963)** commenced as rebel units seized key government installations. Coordinating secretly between **ARVN generals & CIA** operatives, rebel forces captured Diem and his brother Nhu the following morning, resulting in the brutal **assassination of Ngo Dinh Diem** inside an armored vehicle, plunging South Vietnam into years of catastrophic political instability.",
