          "theme_heading": "Publication of the Pentagon Papers",
          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.1]</span> In June 1971, the Nixon administration was rocked by the monumental **Pentagon Papers leak**, published by *The New York Times*. The seven-thousand-page top-secret Department of Defense study had been photocopied and leaked by disillusioned military analyst **Daniel Ellsberg**, exposing decades of systematic deception by the Truman, Eisenhower, Kennedy, and Johnson administrations regarding US political involvement in Southeast Asia.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.2]</span> The documents proved that the White House had covertly planned military escalation and bombing campaigns while publicly promising voters they sought no wider war. Nixon attempted to block publication using prior restraint, but in **New York Times Co. v. United States**, the Supreme Court upheld freedom of the press, confirming to the public that their government had systematically lied about Vietnam.",
