          "act_title": "Stage 2: Operation Frequent Wind & The Fall of Saigon — How did the frantic helicopter evacuations and the fall of Saigon on 30 April 1975 symbolize total American defeat?",
          "title": "Operation Frequent Wind & The Fall of Saigon",
          "theme_heading": "Operation Frequent Wind & The Fall of Saigon",
          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> By late April 1975, eighteen North Vietnamese divisions surrounded Saigon, shelling Tan Son Nhut Airport and cutting all escape routes. On 29 April, the United States launched **Operation Frequent Wind helicopter airlift**, the largest emergency helicopter evacuation in history. Over nineteen hours, Marine helicopters lifted over seven thousand American diplomats and endangered South Vietnamese allies from embassy rooftops to aircraft carriers offshore.\n\n<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> On the morning of 30 April, North Vietnamese tanks crashed through the gates of the presidential compound, completing the **Independence Palace tank capture**. President Duong Van Minh surrendered unconditionally, marking the humiliating **Fall of Saigon (30 April 1975)**. Decades of bloody civil war and American intervention ended in total communist triumph, reunifying the nation as the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.",
